{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Bi Adonai.</b> With alef-dalet (i.e., addressing the divine name Adonai)." "<b>לא איש דברים אנכי.</b> The verse is defective (i.e., its word order is non-sequential), and this is what it says: 'בי Adonai — already <b>מתמול שלשום מאז דברך אל עבדך</b> (since yesterday, since the day before, since You spoke to Your servant)' — I have said to You, 'לא איש דברים אנכי.' And if you wish to explain the words as written, how would you explain it — 'לא איש דברים אנכי מתמול שלשום'? For if he was not a man of words since yesterday, how much more so since the day before; and he should have written in reverse order: 'לא איש דברים אנכי מאז דברך אל עבדך' — neither since the day before nor since yesterday." "<b>גם מאז דברך אל עבדך.</b> Lest you say: from the day You spoke to me I learned to speak fluently." "<b>כי כבד פה.</b> Because I fled from Egypt in my youth, and now I am eighty years old, and I have already forgotten the Egyptian tongue; but Aaron never left there and knows their language."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:07.654427414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}